<title>CANADA: Potash Corp to appeal Kali &amp; Salz ruling.</title>
<headline>Potash Corp to appeal Kali &amp; Salz ruling.</headline>
<dateline>SASKATOON, Saskatchewan 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Potash Corp of Saskatchewan said on Friday that it intends to appeal a German ruling prohibiting Potash Corp's proposed acquisition of a 51 percent stake in Kali und Salz Beteiligungs AG from a unit of BASF AG.</p>
<p>Potash Corp said in a statement German law provides a right to appeal the Federal Cartel Office order both to the German minister of economics and to the courts. &quot;PCS and BASF are preparing and intend to file, as soon as practicable, an application requesting authorization from the German minister of economics for the transaction to proceed,&quot; Potash said.  </p>
<p>Shares in Potash Corp were down 3.35 at 105 in light volume on the Toronto Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>In New York, the company stock dropped 2-3/4 to 76-1/2 on 104,000 shares.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
